  "prompt_text": "Use case: precise-object-edit. Keep this entire wild_boar sprite sheet and transparent cutouts unchanged except tiny interior material marks. Erase existing hatching marks first. Then in EVERY ONE of the TEN animals draw exactly THREE distinct small widely spaced hatch clusters, each containing exactly TWO short parallel slash strokes: clusterA on the SHOULDER, clusterB in the CENTER OF THE FLANK, clusterC on the REAR HAUNCH. Three clusters means six strokes total per animal. Make all three clusters visible in stand, walk, run, head-down forage, and dead positions, BOTH rows. Do not substitute a fur tuft for any interior cluster. Each cluster occupies a small separate region, most body completely unmarked. No grain or extra ticks. Main contour is twice interior line thickness. Preserve exact body shape, all10poses,2row5col layout, colours, broad two-tone wash, projection, light, all connected anatomy. Nothing else changes. Additional person and scene references are locked style only. Actual alpha0 background and wide transparent gutters; no shadows/labels.\n",
